virtiofs: a dax window's page structures made as each range is first mapped

A virtio-fs DAX window's page structures, a 64th of the window, are written whole as the
device is probed (memmap_init_zone_device()), into its head where the device gives one
(0008): a window as long as its host's memory, which a guest that may grow to it (virtio-
mem) could use, cost its guest's boot 1.9 ms and its host 16 MiB a GiB, and a template of
it the save of all of them (shards' PM M306).

A pgmap may leave its pages' structures to its owner (PGMAP_LAZY_MEMMAP), which makes each
range's as it first hands the range out (memmap_init_device_range()), all but the first
page's, whose zone taking the pages down reads; compound pages are made whole, as before.
virtio-fs sets it, and FUSE's DAX makes each 2 MiB range's as the range is first set up
(fuse_setup_one_mapping()), before it is in any inode's tree, so before any fault inserts
its pages: a window costs its guest's boot, and its host, what its guest maps of it.

